  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 120 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nThe aforementioned upper level ridge will remain across the Desert \nSouthwest into the weekend and strengthen. This will result in a \ngradual uptick in temperatures Friday into Saturday. Friday and \nSaturday portions of the area, especially the northern half of the \nforecast area, may reach or exceed Heat Advisory criteria. Highs in \nthese locations will be between 103 and 106 with similar heat index \nvalues. Farther south highs will be in the upper 90s to near 102. \n\nLate Saturday into Sunday, the upper level ridge will inch a bit \nfarther west. This will allow a weak cold front to track south \nacross the region late Saturday into Sunday morning. At this point \nwe are expecting a mainly dry frontal passage. Temperatures will \nstill be hot on Sunday, but a few degrees cooler than forecast highs \non Saturday. Highs will be in the mid 90s to near 102.",
